      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_54ded1521f5b4c4881322b73",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 16, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building address table: one row per address record of a building (a building may hold several addresses for different purposes such as street, mail, parcel, and E911 emergency addresses), with street number and suffix, directional prefixes/suffixes, street name and suffix, city, state, postal code, address purpose, city identifier, and E911 flag. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; used to locate buildings by city/state/street and to report address attributes alongside building characteristics.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"name\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Variant of the historical facilities building snapshot table with the same structure, keys, and coverage as FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (one row per building per fiscal period, FISCAL_PERIOD 201505-201906), differing only in date-column formatting: DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED are stored as DD-MON-YY strings (e.g. '25-APR-03') instead of MM/DD/YYYY. Use FCLT_BUILDING_HIST for building history analysis unless the DD-MON-YY date representation is specifically required.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building address table: one row per building address record per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format), preserving each address's street number/name/suffix, directionals, city, state, postal code, address purpose, and E911 flag over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current address records via FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities floor table: one row per floor per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201602), preserving each floor's number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_FLOOR; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current floor records via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\", \"name\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building snapshot table (FAC_* family): one row per physical building with the same building attribute structure as FCLT_BUILDING (number/name, type, ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates, site, coordinates) but keyed by FAC_BUILDING_KEY and joining the FAC_* family (FAC_ROOMS, FAC_FLOOR, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_ORGANIZATION). Used as the building dimension when FAC_* family keys are involved; FCLT_BUILDING is the counterpart in the FCLT_* family.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FAC_BUILDING\", \"name\": \"FAC_BUILDING\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"name\": \"Building Inventory\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"name\": \"Building Type and Site Classification\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"name\": \"Building Number of Rooms\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"name\": \"Assignable Area Measures\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"name\": \"Access Level Columns\"}]}"
