records, the average number of rooms per historical record, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the total assignable area of the building at MIT, considering only buildings that satisfy all these criteria. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5455\", \"name\": \"MIT Residential Building Minimum Room Count and Average Height with Address Street Number Filter\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"What are the minimum number of rooms and the average building height for each building that is used as a residence, where the number of rooms is between 10 and 400 or the building height is at least 30, and the street number in the building address is between 40 and 27000, and only for buildings at MIT? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
