ORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED (desc: \"without the type/ownership/site classification\") | SUPPORTED but multiplies rows per period (column_concept_building_type_site: \"Filtering on the history columns multiplies result rows\") |\n| Room area measure | FCLT_ROOMS.AREA, square meters | FAC_ROOMS.AREA | ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, square feet | FCLT_ROOMS_HIST covers only period 201505 |\n| Full name | BUILDING_NAME_LONG (\"fuller naming variant\") | same | only BUILDING_NAME | BUILDING_NAME_LONG present |\n| POSTAL_CODE | FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS.POSTAL_CODE (structured) | FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS.POSTAL_CODE | NOT-SUPPORTED (only single-text address fields, per concept_building_address) | FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST (per-period) |\n| Fan-out risk | address join: multiple rows/building (concept_building_address \"Row multiplicity\") | same | one row/building | period duplication |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping.** Atomic requirements: (R1) per-building CV = STDDEV(room area)/AVG(room area); (R2) academic-building filter; (R3) exclude \"Ashdown House\"; (R4) building full name output; (R5) postal code output; (R6) CV > average CV across all academic buildings.\n- FCLT trio: R1 SUPPORTED (FCLT_ROOMS.AREA), R2 SUPPORTED (BUILDING_TYPE), R3 SUPPORTED (BUILDING_NAME; dw_126 precedent literal 'ASHDOWN HOUSE'), R4 SUPPORTED (BUILDING_NAME_LONG), R5 SUPPORTED (POSTAL_CODE), R6 SUPPORTED (two-level aggregation over building-level CVs).\n- FAC trio: all SUPPORTED structurally, but no metric precedent uses FAC_* for room-area statistics (0 precedents found in Phase 1 results).\n- BUILDINGS/SPACE_DETAIL: R2 VIOLATES (no BUILDING_TYPE), R5 VIOLATES (no POSTAL_CODE column).\n- HIST tables: R1 would compute over period-duplicated rows — VIOLATES granularity (\"for each academic building\" = current snapshot per concept_building_inventory decision_guide).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring.** \"academic building\" → `BUILDING_TYPE = 'ACADEMIC'` (column def: \"'ACADEMIC' (academic buildings)\"