ables**: fiscal-period dispersion statistics (dw_1190, dw_505, dw_2596, dw_12).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- FCLT_BUILDING, FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS, FAC_BUILDING, FAC_ROOMS, FAC_BUILDING_ADDRESS, BUILDINGS, SPACE_DETAIL — `semantic_get` (full columns) ✔\n- concept_building_inventory, concept_room_space_inventory, concept_building_address — `semantic_get` (comparisons + decision_guide) ✔; concept_floor_inventory, concept_room_major_use_classification, concept_facility_organization_dimension, concept_space_unit_dimension — screened via search descs; not needed (no floor/use/org requirement in task) ✔\n- column_concept_building_type_site — `semantic_get` ✔; column_concept_assignable_area, column_concept_num_of_rooms, column_concept_access_level, column_concept_building_room — retrieved via graph/search descs; task uses room AREA (not assignable area/num_of_rooms/access level), so documented as non-applicable ✔\n- FCLT_BUILDING graph neighbors + FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS metrics — `semantic_graph` ✔\n- Precedent metrics dw_1888, dw_126, dw_488, dw_1190, dw_565, dw_5455, dw_1488 — `semantic_get` (full SQL) ✔\n- Remaining Phase-1 tables (FCLT_*_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR, FAC_FLOOR, SPACE_FLOOR, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD, SPACE_UNIT, SPACE_USAGE, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FAC_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_MAJOR_USE, FAC_MAJOR_USE, SIS/HR/course tables) — screened; historical/floor/org/course entities do not carry the required current room-area + postal-code + building-type combination; non-facilities tables (departments, terms, TIP/library, Moira, CIP, person directories) are unrelated to the task and discarded ✔\n- `mysql_query` — attempted 6 times; **all failed with server-side auth error `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`**, including `SELECT 1`. Data verification was therefore impossible; the query is grounded in documented column definitions and precedent SQL instead.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** FCLT_BUILDING (`BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC'`, `BUILDING_NAME <> 'ASHDOWN HOUSE'`, `BUILDING_NAME_LONG`, `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY`) ⋈ FCLT_ROOMS (`AREA`) ⋈ FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS (`POSTAL_CODE`).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Two-level aggregation — inner CTE computes per-building `STDDEV(AREA)/AVG(AREA)` grouped by building key + long name (so the address fan-out cannot corrupt the statistics); a second CTE computes `AVG(cv)` over those building-level CVs; the outer query filters `cv > avg_cv` and joins the address table last for POSTAL_CODE (following the discipline of attaching name/address variants after aggregating at the question's granularity). Bare `STDDEV()` per the tip. NULL CVs (single-room buildings, where sample STDDEV is NULL) are naturally excluded by the `>` comparison. No rounding.\n\n**6c. Reasons:**\n- *Data*: FCLT_ROOMS.AREA is the only square-meter room-area column joined one-row-per-room to the current building snapshot; FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS is the only structured POSTAL_CODE source in the family; address join is done post-aggregation to avoid fan-out distorting STDDEV/AVG.\n- *Semantic-network*: concept_building_inventory decision_guide (\"Current building attributes, type/site filters → FCLT_BUILDING\"); concept_room_space_inventory decision_guide (\"Room area statistics in square meters → FCLT_ROOMS\"); concept_building_address decision_guide (\"reporting structured address components (postal code) → FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS\"); column_concept_building_type_site decision_guide (current classification → one row per building).\n- *Business*: dw_1888 precedent computes STDDEV(r.AREA) per academic building on FCLT_BUILDING⋈FCLT_ROOMS; dw_126 precedent supplies the exact exclusion literal `'ASHDOWN HOUSE'` and the avg-comparison CTE pattern; dw_565/dw_126 precedent joins FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS for address attributes. The question lacks \"at MIT\", so no SITE filter is added (unlike dw_488/dw_1888 which explicitly say \"at MIT\").\n\n**6d. Alternatives/tie-breakers:** FAC_* family is structurally equivalent but has zero metric